# title: Vela expressions in operator-grammar form (educational)
# demonstrates: operator precedence parsing (no epsilon, no adjacent nonterminals).
# NOTE: unary minus is the separate terminal 'neg'. With a shared '-' token the precedence
# relations conflict (both < and >), which is why operator-precedence parsing cannot
# separate unary from binary minus. This preset is an educational form of the real grammar,
# not the grammar used by the compiler.
E -> E or A | A
A -> A and N | N
N -> not N | Q
Q -> Q == R | Q != R | R
R -> R < S | R <= S | R > S | R >= S | S
S -> S + T | S - T | T
T -> T * U | T / U | T % U | U
U -> neg U | V
V -> V as int | V as float | V as char | V as string | V as bool | P
P -> ( E ) | id | num
